Now I see the full picture. The bug:

In the desk-event handler (correct):
```js
w.state = 'to_lunch';
w.lunchStart = t;
w.waitFloor = w.floor; w.targetFloor = 0; w.afterRide = 'break';
setPath(w, breakOutPath(w));
```
Sets waitFloor = OFFICE floor (current), targetFloor = 0 (lobby where break area is) ✓ — correct design.

But then in `to_lunch` completion handler (WRONG):
```js
case 'to_lunch':
case 'to_coffee':
  if (waypointReached(w, dt)) {
    w.waitFloor = 0; w.targetFloor = w.floor; w.afterRide = 'desk';
    w.state = 'wait_elev';
  }
```
OVERWRITES with the opposite values! The comment says "walking desk → lobby; on complete → wait at elevator" — the worker walks desk → lobby — wait — but the worker is walking at office-floor altitude?? — the breakOutPath:
```js
function breakOutPath(w) {
  var d = w.desk;   // desk on office floor
  if (d.z > 0) pts = [{x: chair.x, z: 5.55}, {x: 0, z: 5.55}, {x: 0, z: -1.6}];
  else ...
}
```
The waypoints — x/z only — no floor info — the worker is walking in the office — the last waypoint (0, -1.6) is the lobby area... WAIT — the lobby is FLOOR 0 — not the office floor!! The worker walks from the desk (floor N) to (0,-1.6) — physically at floor N? — the waypointReached doesn't change floor — the path is just x/z — the worker walks toward (0,-1.6) while standing at floor N height — that's WRONG — the walk to the lobby should happen at floor N until reaching... — hmm — but the path ends at the lobby (0,-1.6) — physically the lobby is at floor 0.

The intended design (from the summary): "to_lunch/to_coffee entry (desk events) sets waitFloor=w.floor, targetFloor=0, afterRide='break', path=breakOutPath(w); completion → wait_elev (no elevator dispatch here)" — hmm — but then the worker walks at office-floor height to the lobby?? — no wait — the path ends at (0,-1.6) — but where does the worker get DOWN to floor 0? — via the ELEVATOR: the worker waits at floor N (waitFloor=w.floor) at the elevator lobby spot (0,-1.6) — hmm — no — the elevator is IN the office-floor shaft — the wait position (0,-1.55) — the office floors have an elevator lobby — the worker walks from desk to the elevator lobby at floor N — waits at floor N — elevator carries to floor 0 — exits — walks to break point (floor 0) ✓.

So breakOutPath should be: desk → elevator lobby AT OFFICE FLOOR (0,-1.6) — wait — the elevator lobby at floor 0 is the lobby area (z=-1.6 is inside the shaft zone on floor 0?) — hmm — SH_Z0=-6.95, SH_Z1=-2.6 — the shaft is at z -6.95..-2.6 — the wait position z=-1.55 is IN FRONT of the shaft ✓ — on floor 0 (in the lobby area) AND on office floors — the office floors extend z -6.9..6.95 — (0,-1.6) — hmm — z=-1.6 is INSIDE the office floor area — the "shaft lobby" at the office floors — is it there? The office floors are full slabs with the shaft cut out (the shaft region x -2.6..2.6, z -6.95..-2.6) — in front of the shaft (z -2.6..) — the wait position z=-1.55 in front of the shaft ✓ — so (0,-1.6) is in front of the shaft on ANY office floor ✓.

So breakOutPath (desk → wait position at office floor) is correct — the WAIT then happens at floor w.floor — and the elevator carries the worker DOWN to floor 0 — then exits — to_break_point — walks to BREAK_PT (floor 0) ✓.

So the completion handler should NOT overwrite waitFloor/targetFloor — it should just transition to wait_elev KEEPING the values set at entry:
```js
case 'to_lunch':
case 'to_coffee':
  if (waypointReached(w, dt)) { w.state = 'wait_elev'; }
  break;
```
The entries already set waitFloor=w.floor, targetFloor=0, afterRide='break' ✓.

Also check back_from_break:
```js
case 'back_from_break':
  if (waypointReached(w, dt)) {
    w.waitFloor = 0; w.targetFloor = w.floor; w.afterRide = 'desk';
    w.state = 'wait_elev';
  }
```
The worker walks from the break point → to (0,-1.6) (the elevator wait spot) — breakBackPath = [{x:0, z:-1.6}] — walks at FLOOR 0 (currentSurface → to_break_point/break/back_from_break → floor 0 ✓) — then waits at floor 0 — elevator carries to office floor — exit_car → to_desk ✓ — CORRECT — back_from_break keeps waitFloor=0, targetFloor=w.floor ✓.

Also the exit_car handler — let me check it handles afterRide='break' correctly.

